MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural follow-up to Old Sock because the Clapton and JJ Cale connection gives me a familiar route into the relaxed blues sound I want.",
    "Hypnotic Eye connects directly to my interest in You Should Be So Lucky through Benmont Tench and the Heartbreakers; that shared musician makes it more compelling than a broadly similar rock album."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Songs From St. Somewhere has a laid-back feel, but its tropical direction does not give me the blues and roots-rock connection I am looking for now.",
    "No Fools, No Fun is too unfamiliar for me to choose during a quick visit, while CSNY 1974 interests me but asks for more live-album listening than I want today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Familiar rock artists alone are not enough to make every release an immediate choice; I want a specific connection to what I have been hearing.",
    "A relaxed mood can mean very different things to me: Clapton's blues appeals today, but a tropical escape does not."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Direct artist and musician connections matter most today, especially the links from Old Sock to The Breeze and from Benmont Tench to Hypnotic Eye.",
    "I rarely choose many albums in one visit, so finding an album appealing does not mean I will explore it now; the strongest familiar connections take priority."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in familiar blues and roots rock, but some shared only a broad style or mood rather than the direct musical connections that make me choose an album today."
}
